  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836028",
      "title": "Creating Flexible Components with Styled Components",
      "sourceHash": "00ca58cc2b11dd88f11a58a1f45c1fc841544f665c715e522ce934fe178217d3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 1.98,
          "en": "So let's now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.98,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "that the label and the input look good again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "And for that, since I'm now using styled components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "though as you can, of course, see, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "on the header, you can mix and match styled components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 18.63,
          "en": "with other styling approaches like CSS modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "without problems, though typically, you will likely go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 26.58,
          "en": "for one approach that you then use for the entire app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.58,
          "end": 28.653,
          "en": "but you can mix them if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "But here I now wanna dive deeper into styled components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "and therefore, let's now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 37.923,
          "en": "that the label looks good again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "And for that, with our styled components here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "we can, of course, create a label constant starting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "with an uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.49,
          "en": "since it will store a React component inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 55.443,
          "en": "and create it with styled.label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 59.28,
          "en": "Then we need these two back ticks as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.28,
          "end": 61.803,
          "en": "And now we can add our label styles here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.03,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "So for that, in index.css, I'll take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "at which styles were applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 71.73,
          "en": "These styles here in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.73,
          "end": 76.73,
          "en": "and I can copy them and add them here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 82.71000000000001,
          "en": "And now we just have to use this label component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 86.34,
          "en": "instead of the regular label element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.34,
          "end": 91.34,
          "en": "So label like this and like this, and also down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 97.83,
          "en": "And I'll deliberately keep that class name prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.83,
          "end": 100.773,
          "en": "on that styled component here for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 103.95,
          "en": "If I now save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.95,
          "end": 106.92,
          "en": "you'll see that the label looks good again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.92,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "And what you'll also see if I click sign in is that even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.553,
          "en": "that conditional styling still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "but this does now not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "because of some styled components feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 122.56,
          "en": "but because of this dynamically added CSS class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "because that's really important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "about these styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "These components, which you build with styled dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 139.14,
          "en": "do not just use the children prop so that you can wrap them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 141.753,
          "en": "around content like this texture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.59,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "But in addition, they also forward all props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.69,
          "en": "you're setting on this styled component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "to the underlying built-in JSX element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 158.553,
          "en": "So the built-in label in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.53,
          "end": 165.53,
          "en": "So this styled.label creates such a built-in label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 170.57,
          "en": "under the hood and it forwards all props you're setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "on the styled component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 176.31,
          "en": "like this class name prop in this case to that label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.31,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "it's using internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 182.91,
          "en": "It then just also adds these styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 182.91,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "But other than that, it forwards all props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "which, of course, can be super convenient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 192.96,
          "en": "not just for setting a class name here but, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 192.96,
          "end": 194.94,
          "en": "for adding event listeners like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.94,
          "end": 197.163,
          "en": "by setting the onChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.163,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "or for setting the type prop on the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "And that therefore, also makes it super simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "for us to migrate this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 209.678,
          "en": "to styled components, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.678,
          "end": 214.678,
          "en": "All we have to do is create a new constant here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 216.87,
          "en": "which could be named input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.87,
          "end": 221.553,
          "en": "and then use styled input and these back ticks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.82999999999998,
          "end": 227.28,
          "en": "And then search for the styles that should be applied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 227.28,
          "end": 231.34,
          "en": "in this case, these styles here, copy them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 233.04,
          "end": 236.673,
          "en": "and then back in AuthInputs.jsx, add them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 239.07,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "And now we can again use this input component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 244.54,
          "en": "which is based on that styled component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 249.39,
          "en": "as a replacement for the built-in input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 249.39,
          "end": 251.163,
          "en": "Also here for the password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 253.65,
          "end": 256.53,
          "en": "And we don't have to change anything about the props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.53,
          "end": 258.39,
          "en": "Instead this just works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "But we now got all our styling back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 264.153,
          "en": "because we're now properly using styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 267.87,
          "en": "And you see validation works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 267.87,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "and the onChange listener clearly also still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 273.84000000000003,
          "en": "Otherwise, our entered value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 273.84000000000003,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "wouldn't be reflected back into here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 280.563,
          "en": "and validation wouldn't pass after entering a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.49,
          "end": 285.693,
          "en": "So all these props work, but now with styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}